-Rule-based parasitic extraction must evaluate geometries that are absent from a finite characterization set. We propose Full, an observation-conditioned residual model for improving these estimates without increasing the supplied characterization budget. Full combines a numerical anchor, Transformer residuals, and applicable numerical corrections through component-wise gating informed by support geometry and candidate agreement. Learned predictions populate eligible native compute-table entries during preparation, preserving measured values, resistance, runtime lookup, and parasitic-network assembly. A census of 9.89 million OpenRCX calls finds that 55.77\% are raw non-node requests. Across public rules, finite-element data, and cross-process transfer, Full lowers macro normalized root-mean-square error (NRMSE) relative to the OpenRCX kernel and multilinear interpolation with sparse-support extension in all 60 conditions spanning 10--70\% characterization holdout. Fixed-budget comparisons also favor Full over a conditional neural process and component-supervised adapted AttentionCap. In separate fixed-node rule-export experiments, Full improves capacitance and worst-slack fidelity relative to both kernel controls in all 16 layout--budget settings. The compute-table path keeps mean extraction time within 3.5\% of native extraction, with 5.41--13.99\,s of external cold preparation.
